# Provider binaries / module cache — re-created by `terraform init`.
**/.terraform/

# State files can contain resource attribute values (some sensitive) in
# plain text; state belongs in the remote backend, never in Git.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Real variable values, including per-developer overrides. Broad on
# purpose (*.tfvars, not just *.auto.tfvars): terraform.tfvars itself was
# NOT covered before phase 16 (docs/security-review.md), which meant
# nothing stopped a future `git add -A` from picking one up if it ever
# grew a real secret despite the project's convention of keeping tfvars
# non-secret. *.tfvars.example files (see environments/*/terraform.tfvars.example)
# are unaffected — they end in .example, not .tfvars.
*.tfvars
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
crash.log
crash.*.log

# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored — Terraform's own
# guidance is to commit it so provider version selection is reproducible.
